  "definition": "Explicit acknowledgment of sections intentionally absent from a file — Available sections (valid but unused) vs Reserved sections (structurally prohibited in this form)",

  "groups": {
    "available": "Valid for this form but not needed in this file (e.g., Constants — module just doesn't use them)",
    "reserved": "Structurally prohibited in this form (e.g., Modules — belong in lib.rs, not a module file)"
  },

  "why_document_absence": "Undocumented absence raises questions: Is this missing by accident? Reserved Omission answers preemptively — absent on purpose, here's why.",

  "biblical_connection": "God divided light from darkness (Genesis 1:4) — badal applied to documentation. The boundary IS the information.",

